  "description": "PROCESS-ENTER-KEY falls through all five blank-field arms to WHEN OTHER at app/cbl/COUSR01C.cbl:148-150, so IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON at :153 is true and WRITE-USER-SEC-FILE runs. The RESP is NORMAL, which selects :251-259 - four statements whose ORDER is the subtle part. INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS runs FIRST at :252 and blanks the five screen fields and WS-MESSAGE, and only then is the confirmation composed at :255-258. That works solely because SEC-USR-ID lives in WORKING-STORAGE rather than in the map, so it survives the blanking: a translation that composed the message from USERIDI, or that blanked after composing, would put an empty id on the screen and this case would catch it. DFHGREEN reaches ERRMSGC at :254 - the value comes from common.BmsAttributes, reproduced from IBM CICS documentation because DFHBMSCA is absent from this repository, and NOT from any file here. The eleven-row final state is in KEY sequence: app/jcl/DUSRSECJ.jcl STEP02 defines USRSEC as KEYS(8,0) INDEXED, and NEWUSR01 sorts between ADMIN005 and USER0001.",
